<title>BELGIUM: Cobepa surges on Gevaert, Almanij deal.</title>
<headline>Cobepa surges on Gevaert, Almanij deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Belgian holding company Cobepa surged on Monday on news it would buy around half the assets of holding company Gevaert in a deal with holding company Almanij.</p>
<p>Cobepa started up 85 francs, or 5.6 percent, at 1,515 francs before rising to a 1,550 franc life high and then slipping back. At 0815 shares were up 100 francs at 1,530.</p>
<p>Almanij had not yet traded, but bid/ask prices were marked sharply higher at 17,800 francs compared with a close of 15,425 francs last Thursday. At one point bid/ask hit 19,000 francs.</p>
<p>All the companies' shares had been suspended on Friday.</p>
